# Build context exclusions.
#
# Added when the Vite SPA moved into the API image. The `web` stage runs
# `npm ci` and then `COPY frontend/ ./` — without this file that second COPY
# drops the HOST's frontend/node_modules on top of the one npm just installed,
# which is both slow and wrong: a macOS arm64 tree landing in a linux/amd64
# image produces "invalid ELF header" at build time if anything native is
# involved. CI never hits it (a fresh checkout has no node_modules), which is
# the worst kind of difference — it only breaks on the machine you debug on.

# --- never belongs in an image -------------------------------------------
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.venv
*.egg-info

# Built locally, rebuilt by the `web` stage. Copying a stale one in would let a
# forgotten `npm run build` ship instead of the current source.
frontend/dist

# --- data and experiment state -------------------------------------------
# Training data comes from the lake, not the image (commit bd55c0c). The src
# stage's `COPY README.md dataset* ./dataset/` already tolerates its absence —
# README.md is what makes that COPY succeed with nothing to glob.
dataset
mlruns
mlartifacts
*.db

# --- local scratch and tooling -------------------------------------------
.git
.github
.pytest_cache
.vscode
.claude
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
_to_delete
_claude_gate_variant
*.tgz
tests
doc
docs
